  "description": "The Shift Plus i/O 5 is a powerful off-road contender. It is built upon our Plus-size 4-bar linkage i/O frame with 140mm of rear travel and fitted with a new Rockshox Recon RL 140mm Boost fork. The Shift Plus i/O 5 features Shimano's all new E7000 MTB-specific mid-motor, which delivers 250 watts of power and 60 Nm of user-friendly torque with an E8000 504wh battery. A Shimano 10-speed 1X set up keeps shifting simple while Kenda Havoc Pro 27.5\" x 2.6\" Plus-size tires with U-40 double wall rims keep things rolling. The new Tektro 735 4-2 pistons hydraulic disc brakeset delivers a stronger braking performance with oversized 203mm and 180mm discs. The Shift Plus i/O 5 is one of the most versatile yet affordable dual-suspension E-mountain bikes on the market today.\nShift Plus I/O X6 Aluminum frame for Shimano STePS E7000 motor, 140mm travel, tapered head tube\nRockshox Monarch R rear shock w/ LL Tune\nNew RockShox Recon RL, Boost 27.5\"+/29\" Boost fork, 140mm travel, 15mm thru-axle, w/ hydraulic lockout\nNew Shimano STePS E7000 drive unit / 250 Watts / 60Nm Torque, 503 wh STePS E8000 battery\nNew motor-modes switch, New Speed integrated speed sensor\nShimano Deore RD-6000, 10-spd, Shadow Plus rear derailleur, Deore 10-spd, 11-42T cassette\nShimano E7000 crankarms, forged, 34T chainring\nNew Tektro HD-M735 4-2 hydraulic disc brakes, 4-Piston front calipers, 203/180mm rotors",
